    "done_when": "At the committed head: (1) a new module reckon/crew/picker/lane_context.py builds, per offered candidate backend, a return_time block from reckon.crew.run_time_profile.run_time_profile: p50_s and p90_s of wall_seconds for runs matching this node's role and spec level on that backend, the run count, and the size bucket and key used (the node's declared time budget when given, else output tokens); and a budget_source (account-surface, ledger or null) with budget_age_s, marking stale true when a ledger-only reading is older than budget.evidence_shelf_life_minutes. (2) It also builds one local_lane block from reckon.crew.run_time_profile.local_lane_load: running, waiting, headroom, worker_slots, tokens_per_second and read_at, with missing fields as null. (3) reckon/crew/picker/templates/state.jinja renders both blocks, and questions.jinja states that the expected return time for a job of this size, and the local lane's current load, are criteria alongside fit, burn and recent outcomes. (4) tests/test_picker_return_time.py, a new file, passes with ledger rows and lane document synthesised in a temporary directory, covering the return_time figures, the stale marking, nulls for a missing lane document, and a representative nine-candidate state at or under 1,500 tokens (4 characters per token). (5) reckon crew pick --replay 20 runs against live state, and docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/picker-return-time.html publishes the picks, the agreement with the backend actually used, the fallback count, zero refused-model picks, and one rendered state verbatim.\n (6) The representative-state bound in (4) is measured with a congestion block carrying all five keys a real lane reading carries (running, waiting, admission_verdict, stale, slots_state), not a stub. The renderer reaches lane_context from reckon/crew/picker/prompts.py, and this node does not edit reckon/crew/picker/__init__.py, snapshot.py or replay.py, which a concurrent node owns.",
